            "$\\dfrac{11}{5}$",
            "$2$"
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(A) $\\dfrac{9}{5}$",
            "concept": "$f$ is continuous at $x=a$ if LHL $=$ RHL $= f(a)$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Find $f(5)$ and the LHL from the first piece.",
                "math": "f(5) = \\lim_{x \\to 5^-} (kx+1) = 5k + 1"
              },
              {
                "do": "Find the RHL from the second piece.",
                "math": "\\lim_{x \\to 5^+} (3x - 5) = 15 - 5 = 10"
              },
              {
                "do": "For continuity, equate them and solve.",
                "math": "5k + 1 = 10 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; k = \\dfrac{9}{5}",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "So the correct option is (A)."
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Using the $x \\le 5$ piece for both sides; each one-sided limit uses its own piece."
          }
